---
import CodePlayground from './CodePlayground.astro';

// Interactive examples live as real `.eg.astro` files under `../../examples/`.
// They get full Astro editor tooling + `astro check`, and are loaded here as
// raw source strings via Vite's `?raw` query.
import basicNavbarCode from '../../examples/navbar/basic.eg.astro?raw';
import dropdownNavbarCode from '../../examples/navbar/dropdown.eg.astro?raw';
import customClassCode from '../../examples/navbar/custom-class.eg.astro?raw';
import logoOnlyCode from '../../examples/navbar/logo-only.eg.astro?raw';
---

<section class='doc-section'>
  <h2>Basic Navbar</h2>

  <p>
    Create a responsive navigation bar by providing a logo and a list of
    navigation items. The component automatically renders the navigation links
    and includes a call-to-action button.
  </p>

  <CodePlayground code={basicNavbarCode} />
</section>

<section class='doc-section'>
  <h2>Dropdown Navigation</h2>

  <p>
    Set <code>hasDropdown</code> to <code>true</code> on any navigation item to display
    a dropdown indicator. This is useful for menu items that contain additional navigation
    options.
  </p>

  <CodePlayground code={dropdownNavbarCode} />
</section>

<section class='doc-section'>
  <h2>Custom Navigation Styles</h2>

  <p>
    Use the <code>class</code> prop to apply custom Tailwind or CSS utility classes
    to all navigation links, allowing the navbar to match your brand or application
    theme.
  </p>

  <CodePlayground code={customClassCode} />
</section>

<section class='doc-section'>
  <h2>Logo Only</h2>

  <p>
    The navbar can also be used with only a logo. Navigation links are optional,
    making it suitable for landing pages, authentication screens, or simple
    layouts.
  </p>

  <CodePlayground code={logoOnlyCode} />
</section>
